      "content": "That's a good start, but it's a bit too brief for a competitive debate round. My students need more depth than just generalities. Could you break it down into specific, more sophisticated pillars? For example, instead of just saying \"national sovereignty,\" can you elaborate on the philosophical or legal arguments regarding the social contract and a state's duty to its own citizens? I really want them to have a version of the argument that is intellectually rigorous and difficult to dismiss.",
